:: Stairwell_Landing {"position":"200,800","size":"100,100"}
/* =================================================================
   1. INITIALIZATION & SETUP
   Swap UI map to 2nd Floor, update location pin, and check if 
   the player experienced the horrors on the 4th floor.
================================================================= */
<<set $activeMap to "Stairwell 2F">>
<<set $currentLocation to "F2 Entrance">>

/* FIXED: Added $room406_opened to the horrors check */
<<set _sawHorrors to (visited("Unit_401") or $room402_opened or $room405_opened or $room406_opened)>>


/* =================================================================
   2. DESCENT RESOLUTION
   Narrative and stat outcomes based on how they entered the stairs.
================================================================= */
<<if $descentMethod == "quick">>

    You take the stairs two at a time, desperate to put distance between yourself and the 4th floor. Your footsteps echo sharply against the concrete walls. Your momentum is carrying you fast—maybe too fast.
    
    /* --- AGILITY CHECK (Attributes scaled 1-10) --- */
    <<if $agi >= 5>>
        <br><br>
        <span style="color:var(--accent-green);">[AGILITY SUCCESS]</span> 
        In the flickering strobe light, your boot hovers over a slick, dark patch on the stairs. Your reflexes take over. With a surge of adrenaline, you blindly grab the heavy iron handrail, wrenching your shoulder but stopping your fall. You vault over the slick step, landing heavily on the landing below.
    
    <<else>>
        /* Audio: Play violent tumble sound on AGI fail */
        <<run setup.sound.play("tumble", "audio/sfx/stairs_tumble.mp3", false, 1.0)>>
        
        <br><br>
        <span style="color:var(--accent-red);">[AGILITY FAILED]</span> 
        In the strobe-lit darkness, you never see the wet, slick patch coating the steps. 
        <br><br>
        Your heel slides out from under you. The world tilts sickeningly. You violently tumble forward, concrete biting into your ribs and knees. You slam into the metal railing and skid to a halt on the landing below, your lungs burning and your shoulder screaming in pain.
        
        <span style="color:var(--accent-red); font-weight:bold;">-15 HP + HEAVILY DRAINS YOUR STAMINA</span>
        <<set $hp -= 15>>
        <<exert 20>>
        
        /* Animate UI bars downward */
        <<run window.animateStatBar('.bar-fill.hp', $hp, $hp_max)>>
        <<run window.animateStatBar('.bar-fill.stamina', $stamina, $stamina_max)>>
        <<run window.shakeScreen(30)>>
    <</if>>

<<elseif $descentMethod == "slow">>
    You grip the cold iron handrail, taking it one agonizing step at a time. The emergency strobes paint the stairwell in flashes of harsh crimson and pitch black. 
    <br><br>
    As the light flares, the concrete step below you glistens. Something thick and wet is pooling there, dripping slowly over the edge. You press your back against the wall and carefully step wide, avoiding the slick patch entirely.

<<elseif $descentMethod == "flashlight">>
    You flick on your flashlight. Its stark white beam cuts through the oppressive, pulsing red of the emergency lights. 
    <br><br>
    The beam sweeps down the concrete stairs and catches a dark reflection. A thick, wet puddle coats the middle of the flight, trailing down the edges like dark syrup. Keeping the beam steady, you safely navigate around the mess.

<<elseif $descentMethod == "lighter">>
    You flick your lighter. The small, trembling orange flame fights against the oppressive, pulsing red of the emergency strobes, casting wild, dancing shadows against the concrete walls.
    <br><br>
    Holding the flame low, you catch the glint of something wet. A thick puddle coats the middle of the flight, trailing down the steps. It's hard to see the edges in the flickering light, but you manage to carefully step around the worst of it.
<</if>>

<br><br>


/* =================================================================
   3. NARRATIVE REACTION TO THE BLOOD
   Only plays if the player didn't fall down during a 'quick' descent.
================================================================= */
<<if $descentMethod == "slow" or $descentMethod == "flashlight" or $descentMethod == "lighter">>
    
    /* Audio: Play slow, dripping blood loop while observing */
    <<run setup.sound.play("blood_drip", "audio/sfx/blood_drip.mp3", true, 0.6)>>

    You reach the landing and look back up at what you almost stepped in. 
    <br><br>
    It's blood. Arterial, dark, and fresh enough to still be shining.
    <br><br>
    
    <<if _sawHorrors>>
        /* Desensitized reaction */
        After the carnage you left behind in the apartments upstairs, the sight barely registers. The shock has already burned out of your system. You just wipe a stray drop from your shoe and keep moving.
        <br>
        <<chat "You" "image/avatars/player.gif" "left" "Just more blood. Nothing I haven't seen already today.">>
    
    <<else>>
        /* Shocked reaction */
        Your stomach drops. Until now, the nightmare was just a voice on the radio and a text message. But this is real. You feel a sudden, cold spike of dread in your chest.
        <br>
        <<chat "You" "image/avatars/player.gif" "left" "Someone was dragged down these stairs. Recently.">>
        <<set $hum -= 5>>
        /* FIXED: Added UI Ghost Bar animation for Humanity */
        <<run window.animateStatBar('.bar-fill.humanity', $hum, 100)>>
        <br>
        <span style="color:var(--accent-red); font-size:0.85em;">-5 HUMANITY</span>
    <</if>>

<</if>>

<hr style="border-color:#333; margin: 20px 0;">

/* =================================================================
   4. THE BARRICADE (STORY PROGRESSION)
   Forces the player to detour through the 2nd Floor.
================================================================= */
<<set $currentLocation to "F1 Landing">>

You continue your descent, hoping to push straight through to the ground floor lobby. But halfway between the 2nd and 1st floors, the stairs simply end.
<br><br>

<b style="color:var(--accent-gold);">The way down is completely blocked.</b>
<br><br>
Someone dragged heavy oak desks, folding chairs, and a massive glass-front vending machine into the stairwell, wedging them together into an impassable wall of junk. 
<br><br>
There are no bodies here. No blood. Just a desperate, silent testament to whatever the residents were trying to keep from coming up the stairs. And by the look of the dented, buckling metal on the front of the vending machine... 
<br>
<<chat "You" "image/avatars/player.gif" "left" "Whatever was trying to get up was strong. I can't get to the lobby this way.">>
<br>
You have to open the fire door to the 2nd Floor, cross the building, and find the East Wing stairwell.

        <<addObjective "detour_2f" "Cross the 2nd Floor to find the East Wing stairs">> /* Spawns new task */

<div style="margin-top:30px; text-align:center;">
    <<button "Open the door to the 2nd Floor">>
        /* Audio Cleanup: Stop ambient triggers before switching to hallway */
        <<if setup.sound.tracks["blood_drip"]>> <<run setup.sound.stop("blood_drip")>> <</if>>
        <<if setup.sound.tracks["generator_hum"]>> <<run setup.sound.fade("generator_hum", 2000)>> <</if>>
        <<run setup.sound.play("firedoor_click", "audio/sfx/firedoor_click.mp3", false, 0.7)>>
        
        /* --- OBJECTIVE MILESTONE LOGIC --- */
        <<purgeCompleted>> /* Sweeps the completed escape task off the screen instantly */

        /* Transition Setup */
        <<addTime 2>>
        <<set $floorLevel to 2>>
        <<goto "Floor2_Hallway">>
    <</button>>
</div>